.\" jailops-priv.8, installed as /usr/local/share/man/man8/jailops-priv.8
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt JAILOPS-PRIV 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jailops-priv
.Nd the privileged helper of JailOps
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar flags
.Nm
.Op Ar flags
.Cm check-config
.Nm
.Op Ar flags
.Cm hook Ar phase jail
.Nm
.Cm init Fl pool Ar pool
.Op Fl dry-run
.Op Ar flags
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs as root and performs, for
.Xr jailopsd 8 ,
a fixed list of typed operations: ZFS datasets and snapshots below the storage
roots, jails, interfaces and bridges, pf anchors, a few sysctls, downloads of
images and the files the daemon may read.
Everything else is refused, and every request is written to the audit log.
The daemon connects over a unix socket owned by root and the group
.Sy jailops ,
mode 0660; only the configured users and groups may connect.
.Pp
Without a command the helper serves on its socket.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm check-config
Validate the configuration and the storage file, print the effective storage
roots (with the reason a root is inactive), the directories, the interface
prefixes, the admin policy, the fixed binaries and every allow-list.
Inactive roots are warnings: a pool may not be imported yet.
.It Cm hook Ar phase jail
Run one jail hook and exit.
The rendered jail.conf files call this from their exec.* lines;
.Ar phase
is
.Cm prestart , poststart , prestop
or
.Cm poststop .
.It Cm init Fl pool Ar pool
The one-time setup of a host: the user and group, the storage root dataset
.Pa pool/jailops
mounted at
.Pa /jailops ,
the state dataset mounted at
.Pa /var/db/jailops/state
and owned by the daemon's user, the directories, and the two configuration
files.
Everything is idempotent; what exists is left as it is and said so.
Flags:
.Fl dataset ,
.Fl mount ,
.Fl user ,
.Fl group ,
.Fl etc ,
.Fl data-dir ,
.Fl web
(turn the web console on in the daemon's configuration),
.Fl web-address
(its TLS listener, default :39110) and
.Fl dry-run
(say what would be done and do nothing; needs no root).
.It Cm version
Print the version and the protocol version.
.Fl -version
does the same.
.El
.Pp
The flags, which are also the keys of the configuration file:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl config Ar file
The configuration file: lines of
.Ar key No = Ar value
named like the flags.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.conf ;
a missing default file is not an error.
The file must be owned by root and not writable by group or others.
.It Fl socket Ar path
The unix socket, default
.Pa /var/run/jailops/priv.sock .
.It Fl group Ar name , Fl mode Ar octal
The group that owns the socket (default
.Sy jailops )
and its mode (default 0660; others may have no access).
.It Fl allow-user Ar name , Fl allow-group Ar name
A user (the daemon's) or a group allowed to connect.
Repeatable, comma separated.
At least one is required to serve.
.It Fl storage-root Ar dataset
A storage root dataset fixed in the file, for example
.Pa tank/jailops
(repeatable); more are registered at run time and kept in the storage file.
A pool's top dataset is refused unless
.Fl allow-pool-root
is set.
.It Fl storage-file Ar path
The file that persists the storage roots registered at run time, default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.d/storage.conf
(root-owned, mode 0600).
.It Xo
.Fl mount-base Ar dir , Fl state-dir Ar dir ,
.Fl conf-dir Ar dir , Fl work-dir Ar dir
.Xc
The mount point the storage roots are checked against, the state directory
(required; by default
.Pa mount-base/state ) ,
the directory of the rendered jail.conf files (default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/jails )
and the daemon's scratch directory for image builds.
.It Fl helper-path Ar path
The path the jail.conf hooks call, default
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/jailops-priv .
.It Fl if-prefix Ar prefix
An interface name prefix owned by JailOps (default
.Sy jo ) .
.It Fl ndp-proxy Ar uplink=prefix,...
An uplink the IPv6 proxy may use and the prefixes it may answer for
(repeatable).
.It Fl sysctl Ar name , Fl fetch-host Ar host , Fl image-mirror Ar dir
An extra sysctl readable through the helper, a host images may be fetched
from over https, a local directory of image archives.
.It Xo
.Fl admin-raw-param , Fl admin-allow-flag , Fl admin-devfs-ruleset ,
.Fl admin-host-mount , Fl admin-zfs-prop , Fl admin-routes ,
.Fl admin-raw-pf , Fl admin-resume-send
.Xc
The admin policy: what an administrator of the daemon may set beyond the
built-in rules.
.It Fl log Ar stderr | syslog
The audit log destination.
Default stderr, or syslog with
.Fl daemon .
.It Fl pidfile Ar path
Write the process id here.
.It Fl daemon
Detach from the terminal.
The rc.d script uses
.Xr daemon 8
instead.
.It Fl dev
Development: do not require root, allow the invoking user.
.El
.Sh RC.CONF
The rc.d script
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/jailops_priv
runs the helper under
.Xr daemon 8
with
.Fl log Ar syslog ;
it requires
.Sy zfs
and runs before
.Sy jailopsd .
.Bl -tag -width jailops_priv_config
.It Va jailops_priv_enable
Set to
.Dq YES
to start the helper at boot.
.It Va jailops_priv_config
The configuration file.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.conf .
.El
.Pp
The configuration is validated, and the effective roots printed, with
.Dl service jailops_priv checkconfig
and a start refuses a configuration that does not validate.
The storage file is reread with
.Dl service jailops_priv reload
which sends
.Dv SIGHUP .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reread the storage file and verify every storage root again.
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGINT
Stop: the server shuts down and the socket and pidfile are removed.
.It Dv SIGPIPE
Ignored.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.conf
The configuration; the installed sample is
.Pa priv.conf.sample .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.d/storage.conf
The storage roots registered at run time.
.It Pa /var/run/jailops/priv.sock
The socket.
.It Pa /var/run/jailops/priv.pid
The pid of the helper under rc.d.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/jails
The rendered jail.conf files.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/jailops-priv
The binary, called by the jail.conf hooks.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.Cm check-config
exits 0 with a valid configuration even when a storage root is inactive.
.It 1
Not root (without
.Fl dev ) ,
the socket or pidfile could not be made, another helper is listening, or a
hook failed.
.It 2
Usage, an invalid configuration file or storage file, no allowed peer, a
socket mode others may use, or
.Cm init
with bad arguments.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jailops 1 ,
.Xr jail.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr jailopsd 8
